<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins $50 mln Thai turbine contract.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins $50 mln Thai turbine contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French joint venture GEC Alsthom said on Thursday it has won an order worth around $50 million to supply gas and steam turbine generators for a 300 MW combined cycle plant in Thailand.</p>
<p>The two Frame 9E gas turbines and one steam turbine generator will provide electricity and steam to the Rayong Industrial Park at Rayong, 100 km southeast of Bangkok, as well as the grid operated by the Electricity Generating Authority of Thailand. The plant will start operations in summer 1998.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is joinly owned by General Electric Co Plc and Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
